# Whisper-wave Client — Cursor AI Rules

These rules are non-negotiable. Every PR must satisfy them. When in doubt, err
toward extracting to the correct layer rather than keeping code in a component.

---

## 1. Folder Structure — Feature-Slice Architecture

```
src/
  features/
    {domain}/          # e.g. chat, auth, admin, profile, notifications
      api/             # axios/fetch calls only — no business logic
      components/      # React components (.tsx)
      hooks/           # custom hooks (useXxx.ts) + panelTypes.ts
      stores/          # zustand stores
      utils/           # pure functions
      types.ts         # all data-model types for this domain
  shared/
    components/        # reusable UI components
    hooks/             # reusable hooks
    utils/             # pure utility functions
    constants/         # app-wide magic values and config objects
    types/
      index.ts         # barrel — re-exports from sub-files
      user.ts          # User, Avatar, ApiSuccess, notification types
      ui.ts            # shared UI types (EmptyStateProps shape, TabItem, etc.)
      media.ts         # MediaFile, PhotoFilter, SharedLink
      socket.ts        # all socket payload types
      icon.ts          # IconProps
  pages/               # page-level route components only
  layout/              # layout wrappers (AppWrapper, AdminWrapper)
  app/                 # router, providers, queryClient
  socket/              # SocketProvider
```

No other top-level folders under `src/`. No feature code in `pages/`.

---

## 2. Type & Interface Placement — STRICT

### The only type allowed in a .tsx component file:
```tsx
// ONE Props type, directly above its component. Nothing else.
type Props = { ... };
const MyComponent = ({ ... }: Props) => { ... };
```

### Hook files (.ts):
Only a single private `interface Params { ... }` (or equivalent) is allowed for
the hook's own parameter bag. All other types must live in types files.

### All other types go here:
| Type category          | File                                  |
|------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Domain data models     | `features/{domain}/types.ts`          |
| Shared UI shape types  | `shared/types/ui.ts`                  |
| Media/file types       | `shared/types/media.ts`               |
| Socket payload types   | `shared/types/socket.ts`              |
| Icon SVG prop types    | `shared/types/icon.ts`                |
| User/auth types        | `shared/types/user.ts`                |
| Admin-specific types   | `features/admin/types.ts`             |

NEVER define a reusable type inside a .tsx or hook file and import it elsewhere.
If another file needs the type, it belongs in a types file.

---

## 3. Constants & Config

- No magic numbers, string literals, or config objects in component files.
- No inline timeouts, limits, or pixel values without a named constant.
- App-wide constants → `shared/constants/app.ts`
- Route strings → `shared/constants/routes.ts`
- Socket event names → `shared/constants/socketEvents.ts`
- Upload limits/MIME lists → `shared/constants/uploadConfig.ts`
- Feature-scoped constants → `features/{domain}/constants.ts`

```ts
// WRONG — in a component or hook
const debounce = 450;

// RIGHT — in shared/constants/app.ts
export const SEARCH_DEBOUNCE_MS = 450 as const;
```

---

## 4. Separation of Concerns

Components must contain ONLY:
1. Import statements
2. One `Props` type definition
3. JSX (return statement)

Everything else belongs elsewhere:

| Concern              | Location                        |
|----------------------|---------------------------------|
| Business logic       | `hooks/useXxx.ts`               |
| Pure data transforms | `utils/*.ts`                    |
| API calls            | `api/index.ts`                  |
| Global state         | `stores/*.ts` (zustand)         |
| Server state         | hooks via react-query            |

A component may call hooks and pass values to JSX. It must not contain
`useEffect`, `useState`, `useCallback`, or `useMemo` calls directly — extract
to a hook instead.

---

## 5. File Size

Maximum 350 lines per file. If a file exceeds this:
- Extract sub-components into separate files in the same `components/` folder.
- Extract logic into a dedicated hook.
- Split a large hook into smaller, focused hooks.

---

## 6. Pure Utilities — No Side Effects

Functions in any `utils/` file must be pure:
- No `toast(...)` calls
- No `navigate(...)` calls
- No React hook calls (`useState`, `useEffect`, etc.)
- No direct DOM access
- Same input always produces same output

Side effects belong in hooks or event handlers in components.

---

## 7. Context Menu Pattern

Always attach behavior via `onClick` on option objects. Never dispatch by id or
name string inside a generic handler.

```ts
// CORRECT
const options = [
  { label: 'Delete', icon: <TrashIcon />, onClick: () => handleDelete(id), danger: true },
  { label: 'Copy',   icon: <CopyIcon />,  onClick: () => handleCopy(id) },
];

// WRONG — dispatching by string inside a shared handler
const handleAction = (actionName: string) => {
  if (actionName === 'delete') handleDelete(id);
  if (actionName === 'copy') handleCopy(id);
};
```

---

## 8. Exports from Component Files

A `.tsx` file may only export:
- The default React component
- Its `Props` type (for use by a direct parent only)

NEVER import a type from a `.tsx` file in any other module. If the type is
needed elsewhere, move it to the appropriate `types.ts` file and import from
there.

---

## 9. Custom Hooks

- Every custom hook must start with `use` (e.g., `useChatScroll`, not
  `chatScroll` or `getChatScroll`).
- Any logic in a component body that has more than one line or uses a hook
  primitive must be extracted into a custom hook.
- Hook files live in `features/{domain}/hooks/` or `shared/hooks/`.

---

## 10. Naming Conventions

| Thing              | Convention             | Example                    |
|--------------------|------------------------|----------------------------|
| Components         | PascalCase             | `MessageBubble.tsx`        |
| Hooks              | camelCase with `use`   | `useChatScroll.ts`         |
| Utility functions  | camelCase              | `formatFileSize`           |
| Constants objects  | SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE   | `UPLOAD_CONFIG`            |
| Scalar constants   | SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE   | `MAX_FILES`                |
| Folders            | kebab-case             | `context-menu/`, `image-viewer/` |
| Type files         | lowercase              | `types.ts`, `ui.ts`        |

---

## 11. No console.log in Production Code

Remove all `console.log`, `console.warn`, and `console.error` calls before
committing. Use a logger abstraction or remove entirely.

---

## 12. Admin Types Isolation

All admin-domain types must live in `features/admin/types.ts`.
Never define `AdminUserRow`, `AdminGroupRow`, `AdminMessageRow`, or any admin
type in a component file, hook file, or shared types file.
